'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  e7-workaround-hub-access-test.spin2
''   Purpose....  Erratum E7 workaround test: whether a RDLONG, or a
''                WRLONG and the RDLONG after it, started 16 clocks after
''                a no-wait RDFAST complete with their own hub access in
''                every hub alignment; the waiting form with no spacing;
''                WRBYTE and WRWORD after the same spacing; alongside, the
''                unspaced read and write that show the erratum
''   Manual.....  P2 Errata
''   Version....  v0.3.0 (2026-10-03)
''   Appears in.  Appendix A: How Each Erratum Was Confirmed
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. It is the whole
''   program the chapters listed above name; where the manual
''   quotes it, it quotes excerpts.
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS MEASURED

  Erratum E7: after a no-wait RDFAST (D[31] = 1), a hub instruction
  started fewer than 16 clocks after the start of the RDFAST can complete
  before its own hub access.  A RDLONG then returns the long of the
  previous hub read, with the flags of that long; a WRLONG followed at
  once by a RDLONG of the same address can lose its write.  The waiting
  form (D[31] = 0) completes nothing early.

  This program runs the three workaround blocks the E7 chapter prints,
  each exactly as printed, in all 64 hub alignments, 16 times each:
    W_READ   no-wait RDFAST / WAITX #HUB_SPACING_WAITX / RDLONG ... WCZ
    W_WRITE  no-wait RDFAST / WAITX #HUB_SPACING_WAITX / WRLONG / RDLONG
    W_WAIT   waiting RDFAST / WRLONG / RDLONG ... WCZ   (no spacing)
  A no-wait RDFAST takes 2 clocks and WAITX #12 takes 2 + 12, so in
  W_READ and W_WRITE the first hub instruction after the RDFAST starts
  16 clocks after the RDFAST starts.  Alongside, not printed: WRBYTE at
  byte offsets 0..3 and WRWORD at offsets 0 and 2 after the same
  spacing.  In the same run: two positive controls that reproduce the
  erratum with no spacing, and four controls that prove the rig.

  The program compiles WITH debug (pnut-ts -d) and confines the debugger
  to cog 0 (DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001).  The measuring cog has no debug
  interrupt, no debug() and no BRK, and sets up no interrupt.  Cog 0 only
  polls the mailbox while the measuring cog runs, and each cog has its own
  hub slot.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.  Cog 0
  (Spin2) fills the hub data, sends one command per run, waits for the
  measuring cog (1 s timeout), classifies the records from hub RAM and
  prints them.  The measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution, PASM below)
  runs every trial from cog RAM, so no instruction fetch from hub comes
  between the instructions under test.  Every trial is its own
  hand-written copy.
  After the records of every run, the measuring cog writes back the value
  its nowait register held (MB_ECHO); cog 0 prints RIG FAIL and ends the
  run if it is not $8000_0000.

HUB LAYOUT (constant addresses, all below the last 16 KB at $7_C000,
  which holds the debugger and can be write-protected; the program image,
  its VAR space and cog 0's stack sit far below $4_0000 - main() checks
  the stack address at run time and prints RIG FAIL if it is not at least
  16 KB below $4_0000)
    $4_0000  stream source, 64 longs, long k = $1E1E_0000 + k (never
             expected in a record: a record holding one shows F)
    $4_1000  read table: 8 sentinel longs $5A5A_0002, slot bits 0..7
    $4_2000  write targets: 8 longs, slot bits 0..7
    $4_3000  primer long $A5A5_0001, slot bits 0
    $4_4000  records: 1,024 trials x 3 longs, to $4_6FFF
  Every region starts on a 32-byte boundary, so long k of a region has
  slot bits k mod 8.  Cog 0 fills the record area with $EEEE_EEEE before
  every run, so a record the measuring cog never wrote shows U.

ONE TRIAL (measuring cog, cog execution)
  image R (the reads):
    value := seed $C3C3_0003 ; flags := $FF (no WCZ)
    modcz _set, _set wcz            C=1 Z=1 (only trials whose RDLONG has
                                    WCZ: a missing flag write shows)
    rdlong tmp, primer              the last hub read is now $A5A5_0001,
                                    and the cog's hub phase is set
    the run's instructions          (RUNS, below)
    wrc / bitz                      C and Z into flags (WCZ trials only)
    settle (100 x djnz, >= 200 clocks) ; rdlong later, hub_addr
    record value, later, flags
  image W (the writes):
    wrlong old, target ; settle ; check := later := seed ;
    value := the write data ; flags := $FF
    [modcz _set, _set wcz]          W_WAIT only
    rdlong tmp, primer
    the run's instructions
    [wrc / bitz]                    W_WAIT only
    settle ; rdlong later, target ; record check, later, flags
  hub_stream = $4_0000 + 4*af.  Image R: hub_addr = $4_1000 + 4*a.
  Image W: hub_long = $4_2000 + 4*a, the target long; hub_addr = hub_long
  + the byte offset (0 for the long writes).  The read-back reads the
  whole long at hub_long.
  From the primer to the last instruction under test there is nothing
  but the run's instructions; no ## operand there (it would add an AUGS).
  Repetition r, cell (af, a): record r*64 + af*8 + a.  16 repetitions of
  all 64 cells per run: 1,024 records.  delta = (a - af) mod 8.

RUNS, IN ORDER.  PREDICTIONS ARE SET DOWN HERE AND PRINTED BEFORE THE
  FIRST RUN
   K_CLK    getct / waitx #HUB_SPACING_WAITX / getct            CONTROL
            MUST: elapsed 16 (GETCT 2 + WAITX 2+12) in all 1,024.
   C1       preset / primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST /
            rdlong value, hub_addr wcz                          CONTROL
            MUST: the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1,024.
   PS       primer / rdfast nowait, hub_stream / waitx #200 /
            rflong value                                        CONTROL
            MUST: the stream's first long, $1E1E_0000 + af, in all
            1,024: the RDFAST under test, with the register and the
            addresses the runs use, starts a stream at its address.
   C3       primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST /
            wrlong value, hub_addr / rdlong check, hub_addr     CONTROL
            MUST: (new,new) in all 1,024.
   P_READ   preset / primer / rdfast nowait, hub_stream /
            rdlong value, hub_addr wcz                 POSITIVE CONTROL
            PREDICT per repetition: 43 cells the primer with C=1 Z=0,
            by delta 0..7 = 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2; the other 21 the sentinel
            with C=0 Z=0.
   W_READ   preset / primer / the printed read block       WORKAROUND
            PREDICT: the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1,024.
   P_WRITE  primer / rdfast nowait, hub_stream /
            wrlong value, hub_addr / rdlong check, hub_addr
                                                       POSITIVE CONTROL
            PREDICT per repetition: 43 cells (old,old) - the write lost
            - by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2, and 21 (primer,new) - the write
            landed, the read-back completed early.
   W_WRITE  primer / the printed write block               WORKAROUND
            PREDICT: (new,new) in all 1,024.
   W_WAIT   preset / primer / the printed waiting-form block
                                                           WORKAROUND
            PREDICT: (new,new) with C=1 Z=0, the new long's flags, in
            all 1,024.
   W_WRBYTE+0..+3, W_WRWORD+0, W_WRWORD+2
            primer / rdfast nowait, hub_stream /
            waitx #HUB_SPACING_WAITX / wrbyte (wrword) value, hub_addr /
            rdlong check, hub_long.  Old long $4C3D_2E1F, write data
            $C8D9_EAFB (WRBYTE writes $FB, WRWORD $EAFB).
            PREDICT: the merged long, read back at once and read later,
            in all 1,024 records of each run:
              WRBYTE +0 $4C3D_2EFB  +1 $4C3D_FB1F  +2 $4CFB_2E1F
                     +3 $FB3D_2E1F
              WRWORD +0 $4C3D_EAFB  +2 $EAFB_2E1F
  Values: primer $A5A5_0001, sentinel $5A5A_0002, seed $C3C3_0003, old
  $0F0F_0004, new $F0F0_0005.  C of a RDLONG ... WC is bit 31 of the
  long, Z is "the long is zero": the primer and the new long give C=1
  Z=0, the sentinel and the old long C=0 Z=0, the preset C=1 Z=1.

RECORD CODES (printed per cell for repetition 0)
  image R cell: the code of value, then the flags code
  image W cell: the code of check, of later, then the flags code
  value codes: O old  N new (the long the write should leave)  P primer
     S sentinel  D seed (never written)  F a stream long  U $EEEE_EEEE
     (never written)  X other  . right (K_CLK 16 clocks; PS the stream's
     first long)
  flags code: C + 2*Z as a digit, - no WCZ in the trial, U never
     written, ? other
  agree code per cell: "." = all 16 repetitions identical, else the
     number (hex) of repetitions identical to repetition 0.
  Each run prints its rows, its totals, every cell not clean in some
  repetition with that count (af a:count), and its first record not
  clean (for P_READ and P_WRITE: its first record the prediction does
  not name).

GATES (each failure prints RIG FAIL; every verdict then prints NO VERDICT)
  Ending the run at once: hub layout (checked before any data is written),
       measuring cog start-up or done-flag timeout, a nowait echo that is
       not $8000_0000.
  After the runs: any record left $EEEE_EEEE in any run; any image R
       later read (the table long, after settling) not the sentinel;
       K_CLK, C1, PS or C3 not right in all 1,024 records (this also
       catches an unnamed value and disagreeing repetitions in a
       control).
  POSITIVE CONTROLS (same run; a workaround verdict counts only if its
  control reproduced the erratum):
       P_READ reproduced: every record the primer with C=1 Z=0 or the
       sentinel with C=0 Z=0, every cell's 16 repetitions identical, 43
       primer cells by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2.
       P_WRITE reproduced: every record (old,old) or (primer,new), every
       cell's 16 repetitions identical, 43 (old,old) cells by delta
       8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 and 21 (primer,new).

VERDICTS (printed last), each decided in the order listed
  VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ:  (W_READ; gated on P_READ)
    NO VERDICT    a gate failed
    REFUTED       a W_READ record not the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 (the
                  count, the cells and the first such record printed)
    INCONCLUSIVE  W_READ clean, but P_READ did not reproduce the erratum
    CONFIRMED     the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1,024 records
  VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE:  (W_WRITE; gated on P_WRITE)
    NO VERDICT / REFUTED (a record not (new,new)) / INCONCLUSIVE /
    CONFIRMED ((new,new) in all 1,024)
  VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING:  (W_WAIT; gated on P_WRITE)
    NO VERDICT / REFUTED (a record not (new,new) with C=1 Z=0) /
    INCONCLUSIVE / CONFIRMED
  VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES:  (the six runs; gated on
    P_WRITE)  NO VERDICT / REFUTED (a record not the merged long; the
    count per run printed) / INCONCLUSIVE / CONFIRMED

OPCODES (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the .lst hub
  image; object offset = cog address * 4 + $F0).  RDFAST is 1100011 1LI,
  WRLONG 1100011 0LI, WRBYTE 1100010 0LI, WRWORD 1100010 1LI, RDLONG
  1011000 CZI, NOP $0000_0000.  Cog registers: nowait $0A7, hub_stream
  $0A8, hub_addr $0A9, hub_long $0AA, value $0AB, check $0AC, c_prim
  $0B0, c_flags $0B7, c_tmp $0C2; the cog image ends at c_tmp (pasm_end
  $0C3).
    modcz _set,_set wcz          $FD7DFE6F  flags preset C=1 Z=1
    rdlong c_tmp,c_prim          $FB0184B0  the primer (every copy)
    rdfast nowait,hub_stream     $FC714EA8  L=0 I=0: D = register nowait
                                            ($8000_0000: no-wait)
    waitx #HUB_SPACING_WAITX     $FD64181F  L=1, D = 12: no AUGS
    rdlong value,hub_addr wcz    $FB1956A9  C1, P_READ, W_READ
    wrlong value,hub_addr        $FC6156A9  C3, P_WRITE, W_WRITE, W_WAIT
    rdlong check,hub_addr        $FB0158A9  C3, P_WRITE, W_WRITE
    rdfast #0,hub_stream         $FC7800A8  L=1 D=#0: the waiting form
    rdlong check,hub_addr wcz    $FB1958A9  W_WAIT
    wrbyte value,hub_addr        $FC4156A9  W_WRBYTE
    wrword value,hub_addr        $FC5156A9  W_WRWORD
    rdlong check,hub_long        $FB0158AA  W_WRBYTE, W_WRWORD
    waitx #200 / rflong value    $FD65901F / $FD615612  PS only
    wrc c_flags / bitz c_flags,#1  $FD616E6C / $F4856E01
    wrlong nowait,ptra[MB_ECHO]  $FC654F06  at cmd_done ($124), after
                                            every record of the run
  Adjacency read from the image (object offsets):
    K_CLK    $1B0 getct, $1B4 waitx #12, $1B8 getct
    C1       $1C8 modcz, $1CC primer, $1D0 nop, $1D4 rdlong wcz
    PS       $1E4 primer, $1E8 rdfast, $1EC waitx #200, $1F0 rflong
    P_READ   $1F8 modcz, $1FC primer, $200 rdfast, $204 rdlong wcz
    W_READ   $214 modcz, $218 primer, $21C rdfast, $220 waitx #12,
             $224 rdlong wcz                       (the printed block)
    C3       $2D0 primer, $2D4 nop, $2D8 wrlong, $2DC rdlong
    P_WRITE  $2E4 primer, $2E8 rdfast, $2EC wrlong, $2F0 rdlong
    W_WRITE  $2F8 primer, $2FC rdfast, $300 waitx #12, $304 wrlong,
             $308 rdlong                           (the printed block)
    W_WAIT   $310 modcz, $314 primer, $318 rdfast #0, $31C wrlong,
             $320 rdlong wcz                       (the printed block)
    W_WRBYTE $330 primer, $334 rdfast, $338 waitx #12, $33C wrbyte,
             $340 rdlong
    W_WRWORD $348 primer, $34C rdfast, $350 waitx #12, $354 wrword,
             $358 rdlong
  In W_READ and W_WRITE the hub instruction after the RDFAST issues
  2 (RDFAST) + 14 (WAITX #12) = 16 clocks after the RDFAST issues; K_CLK
  measures the WAITX on the part.
  DEBUG OUTPUT.  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub
  strings and numbers and sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in
  ln_out(); the only other record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The
  listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.

HOW TO RUN
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or
  PNut Ctrl-F10).  Runs once; nothing written to flash.  Output: header
  with every prediction, one block per run (rows + totals), GATES, the
  two POSITIVE CONTROL lines, RESULTS, the four VERDICT lines, then
  DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000         ' system clock: 200 MHz
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

' ---- E7 WORKAROUND SPACING: begin (Erratum E7 prints this line) ----
  HUB_SPACING_WAITX = 12                ' RDFAST 2 + WAITX 2+12 = 16 clocks
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND SPACING: end ----

  NSLOT           = 8                   ' slot bits: address bits [4:2]
  NCELL           = NSLOT * NSLOT       ' (af, a) cells per repetition
  REPS            = 16                  ' repetitions of every cell per run
  NREC            = REPS * NCELL        ' records (trials) per run: 1,024
  RECW            = 3                   ' longs per record: v1, v2, flags
  SETTLE_N        = 100                 ' DJNZ count of a settle loop: >= 200 clocks
  STREAM_WAIT     = 200                 ' PS: WAITX between the no-wait RDFAST and its RFLONG

  GETCT_OVH       = 2                   ' GETCT-pair overhead
  WAITX_BASE      = 2                   ' WAITX D costs 2 + D
  RDFAST_CLK      = 2                   ' a no-wait RDFAST takes 2 clocks
  CLK_PRED        = GETCT_OVH + WAITX_BASE + HUB_SPACING_WAITX   ' K_CLK elapsed: 16
  SPACING_CLK     = RDFAST_CLK + WAITX_BASE + HUB_SPACING_WAITX  ' RDFAST start to next start: 16

  PRIMV           = $A5A5_0001          ' primer: the last hub read before the RDFAST
  SENTV           = $5A5A_0002          ' sentinel: the read table's longs
  SEEDV           = $C3C3_0003          ' seed: a register before the trial ("never written")
  OLDV            = $0F0F_0004          ' long writes: the target before the trial
  NEWV            = $F0F0_0005          ' long writes: what the WRLONG writes
  OLDBW           = $4C3D_2E1F          ' byte / word writes: the target before the trial
  DATABW          = $C8D9_EAFB          ' byte / word writes: the data register (byte $FB, word $EAFB)
  STRM_V          = $1E1E_0000          ' stream region long k = STRM_V + k
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' record-area fill: nothing written here
  FIFO_NO_WAIT    = $8000_0000          ' the nowait register: D[31]=1 no-wait, block count 0

  LONG_MSB        = 31                  ' C of a RDLONG WC = bit 31 of the long
  FLAG_Z_BIT      = 1                   ' flags record: bit 0 = C, bit 1 = Z
  FLAG_CODES      = 4                   ' flags record values 0..3 (C + 2*Z)
  FLAGS_NONE      = $FF                 ' flags record of a trial with no WCZ
  BITS_PER_BYTE   = 8
  SIZE_BYTE       = 1                   ' write sizes in bytes
  SIZE_WORD       = 2
  SIZE_LONG       = 4

  PRED_REL        = 43                  ' positive controls: released cells per repetition
  PRED_RDREL      = 21                  ' P_WRITE: (primer,new) cells per repetition
  NCTRL           = 4                   ' gating controls: K_CLK, C1, PS, C3

  ' -- constant hub layout (HUB LAYOUT in the header) --
  HUB_STRM        = $4_0000             ' stream source, slot 0 aligned
  STRM_LONGS      = 64
  HUB_TBL         = $4_1000             ' read table: sentinels
  HUB_WTBL        = $4_2000             ' write targets
  HUB_PRIM        = $4_3000             ' primer long
  HUB_RES         = $4_4000             ' records
  HUB_DATA_LO     = HUB_STRM            ' lowest data byte
  HUB_DATA_END    = HUB_RES + NREC * RECW * 4   ' first byte above the data ($4_7000)
  HUB_TOP16K      = $7_C000             ' the last 16 KB of hub RAM starts here
  STACK_MARGIN    = $4000               ' room demanded between cog 0's stack and the data

  STAT_READY      = $0000_0A11          ' measuring cog is up
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars); longer text is cut
  R_CELL_W        = 3                   ' row chars per image R cell: value, flags, space
  W_CELL_W        = 4                   ' row chars per image W cell: check, later, flags, space

  SUCCESS         = 0
  E_RIG_FAIL      = -1                  ' the measuring cog did not answer within 1 s
  E_MODE_FAIL     = -2                  ' the nowait echo is not $8000_0000

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' commands to the measuring cog (MB_CMD)
  #1, CMD_R, CMD_W

  ' runs, in run order
  #0, RUN_KCLK, RUN_C1, RUN_PS, RUN_C3, RUN_PREAD, RUN_WREAD, RUN_PWRITE, RUN_WWRITE, RUN_WWAIT
  RUN_WB0         = RUN_WWAIT + 1       ' W_WRBYTE+0 .. +3
  RUN_WB3         = RUN_WB0 + 3
  RUN_WW0         = RUN_WB3 + 1         ' W_WRWORD+0
  RUN_WW2         = RUN_WW0 + 1         ' W_WRWORD+2
  NRUN            = RUN_WW2 + 1

  ' trial copies in the measuring cog (rvec_tab, wvec_tab order)
  #0, RCOPY_KCLK, RCOPY_C1, RCOPY_PS, RCOPY_PREAD, RCOPY_WREAD
  #0, WCOPY_C3, WCOPY_PWRITE, WCOPY_WWRITE, WCOPY_WWAIT, WCOPY_WBYTE, WCOPY_WWORD

  ' value classes (printed codes O N P D S F U X .)
  #0, VC_OLD, VC_NEW, VC_PRIM, VC_SEED, VC_SENT, VC_STRM, VC_UNWR, VC_OTHER, VC_RIGHT

  ' record kinds:
  '  KD_CLEAN - what the run predicts when nothing completes early (a control's MUST)
  '  KD_REL   - completed early: image R the primer; image W (old,old), the write lost
  '  KD_RDREL - image W (primer,new): the write landed, the read-back completed early
  '  KD_OTHER - anything the prediction does not name
  #0, KD_CLEAN, KD_REL, KD_RDREL, KD_OTHER
  NKIND           = KD_OTHER + 1

  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> measuring cog)
  '  MB_CMD   - 0 idle / CMD_*; the measuring cog writes 0 when done
  '  MB_COPY  - trial copy (RCOPY_* / WCOPY_*)
  '  MB_OLD   - image W: the long the target holds before the trial
  '  MB_WVAL  - image W: the write data register
  '  MB_OFFS  - image W: byte offset of the write in the target long
  '  MB_ALIVE - STAT_READY once the measuring cog runs
  '  MB_ECHO  - the nowait register's value, written back after the records
  #0, MB_CMD, MB_COPY, MB_OLD, MB_WVAL, MB_OFFS, MB_ALIVE, MB_ECHO, MB_LEN

  ' record longs
  #0, REC_V1, REC_V2, REC_FL

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  ' per run
  long kindCnt[NRUN * NKIND]            ' records per kind over all repetitions
  long rep0Kind[NRUN * NKIND]           ' repetition-0 cells per kind
  long runDelta[NRUN * NSLOT]           ' repetition-0 KD_REL cells by delta
  long runDisagree[NRUN]                ' cells whose 16 repetitions are not identical
  long runBadCells[NRUN]                ' cells not clean in some repetition
  long runUnwr[NRUN]                    ' records with a long still $EEEE_EEEE
  long runTableBad[NRUN]                ' image R: later read not the sentinel
  long runEcho[NRUN]                    ' the nowait register's value, echoed back
  long runBadRec[NRUN], runBadV1[NRUN], runBadV2[NRUN], runBadFl[NRUN]   ' first record not clean
  long runOthRec[NRUN], runOthV1[NRUN], runOthV2[NRUN], runOthFl[NRUN]   ' first record of KD_OTHER
  long runDamage                        ' data longs changed during the runs
  long clkMin, clkMax                   ' K_CLK elapsed range
  ' the run being processed, per cell (repetition 0)
  byte cellV1[NCELL], cellV2[NCELL], cellFl[NCELL], cellAgree[NCELL], cellNotClean[NCELL]
  ' print buffers
  byte rowStr[NSLOT * W_CELL_W + 1]
  byte agreeStr[NSLOT + 1]
  ' every printed line is built here and sent by ONE debug() record (ln_out)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | runIdx, cog, startCt, status, pStack, damageCnt, bRigOk, bReadRepro, bWriteRepro
'' Run every run on the measuring cog, print the raw rows, then the gates,
'' the positive controls and the verdicts.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @local cog - cog the measuring cog started in
' @local startCt - CT at the start of the start-up timeout
' @local status - SUCCESS, E_RIG_FAIL or E_MODE_FAIL
' @local pStack - hub address of this method's locals: cog 0's stack
' @local damageCnt - data longs changed by the run just made
' @local bRigOk - every gate passed
' @local bReadRepro - P_READ reproduced the erratum
' @local bWriteRepro - P_WRITE reproduced the erratum

  pStack := @status
  linePos := 0
  ' the layout check runs before the first write to the data area it protects
  if pStack + STACK_MARGIN > HUB_DATA_LO or HUB_DATA_END > HUB_TOP16K
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: hub layout - cog 0 stack at "))
    ln_h(pStack)
    ln_s(string(" must lie at least "))
    ln_h(STACK_MARGIN)
    ln_s(string(" below the data at "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_LO)
    ln_s(string(", and the data end "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
    ln_s(string(" must lie below "))
    ln_h(HUB_TOP16K)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  reset_tallies()
  fill_regions()
  mbox[MB_CMD] := 0
  mbox[MB_ALIVE] := 0

  print_header(pStack)

  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if cog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(cog)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_ALIVE] == STAT_READY
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog start-up expected $0000_0A11 within 1 s, got "))
      ln_h(mbox[MB_ALIVE])
      ln_out()
      finish()
  ln_s(string("measuring cog "))
  ln_d(cog)
  say(string(" running"))

  repeat runIdx from 0 to NRUN - 1
    print_run_header(runIdx)
    longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, NREC * RECW)
    status := send_cmd(runIdx)
    if status == E_RIG_FAIL
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not finish run "))
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      say(string(" within 1 s (done flag never cleared)"))
    if status <> SUCCESS
      finish()
    runEcho[runIdx] := mbox[MB_ECHO]
    process_run(runIdx)
    print_run(runIdx)
    damageCnt := region_damage()
    if damageCnt > 0
      runDamage += damageCnt
      ln_s(string("  REGION DAMAGE after "))
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      ln_s(string(": "))
      ln_d(damageCnt)
      say(string(" data longs changed (a stray hub write) - regions re-filled"))
      fill_regions()

  say(string("=== GATES ==="))
  bRigOk := rig_gate()
  bReadRepro := pos_read()
  bWriteRepro := pos_write()

  say(string("=== RESULTS ==="))
  verdict_read(bRigOk, bReadRepro)
  verdict_write(bRigOk, bWriteRepro)
  verdict_waiting(bRigOk, bWriteRepro)
  verdict_bytes(bRigOk, bWriteRepro)

  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_d(numVal) | divisor, bStarted
' Append a signed decimal (the form udec_/sdec_ printed) to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  if numVal == NEGX
    ln_s(string("-2147483648"))
  else
    if numVal < 0
      ln_c("-")
      numVal := -numVal
    divisor := 1_000_000_000
    bStarted := FALSE
    repeat 10
      if numVal >= divisor or bStarted or divisor == 1
        ln_c("0" + numVal / divisor)
        numVal //= divisor
        bStarted := TRUE
      divisor /= 10

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as uhex_long_ printed it: $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from 7 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)
    if idx == 4
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_row8(pLongs) | idx
' Append 8 longs as decimals separated by single spaces.
'
' @param pLongs - hub address of the first long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index 0..7

  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if idx > 0
      ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(long[pLongs][idx])

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI ln_waitx()
' Append "waitx #<HUB_SPACING_WAITX>".
'

  ln_s(string("waitx #"))
  ln_d(HUB_SPACING_WAITX)

PRI ln_run(runIdx)
' Append "  <run name>", the lead of every per-run line.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(run_name(runIdx))

PRI ln_fl(recFl)
' Append a flags record: its code, or its hex value when it is not a code.
'
' @param recFl - the flags long of a record

  if flchar(recFl) == "?"
    ln_h(recFl)
  else
    ln_c(flchar(recFl))

PRI ln_rec(recIdx, recV1, recV2, recFl)
' Append one record: "rep r af f a n: v1 $.. v2 $.. flags c".
'
' @param recIdx - record index: rep * 64 + af * 8 + a
' @param recV1 - the record's first long
' @param recV2 - the record's second long
' @param recFl - the flags long of a record

  ln_s(string("rep "))
  ln_d(recIdx / NCELL)
  ln_s(string(" af "))
  ln_d((recIdx // NCELL) / NSLOT)
  ln_s(string(" a "))
  ln_d(recIdx // NSLOT)
  ln_s(string(": v1 "))
  ln_h(recV1)
  ln_s(string(" v2 "))
  ln_h(recV2)
  ln_s(string(" flags "))
  ln_fl(recFl)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' set-up and the command channel
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header(pStack) | runIdx
' Print the rig identity, the hub layout and every prediction before the run.
'
' @param pStack - hub address of main()'s locals (cog 0's stack)

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

  say(string("=== P2 Errata, Erratum E7 workarounds: hub reads and writes after a no-wait RDFAST (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz) ==="))
  say(string("values: primer $A5A5_0001  sentinel $5A5A_0002  seed $C3C3_0003  old $0F0F_0004  new $F0F0_0005  stream long k $1E1E_0000+k  unwritten $EEEE_EEEE"))
  ln_s(string("byte/word writes: old $4C3D_2E1F, data $C8D9_EAFB; the merged long each leaves:"))
  repeat runIdx from RUN_WB0 to RUN_WW2
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(run_new(runIdx))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("hub: stream "))
  ln_h(HUB_STRM)
  ln_s(string(" read table "))
  ln_h(HUB_TBL)
  ln_s(string(" write targets "))
  ln_h(HUB_WTBL)
  ln_s(string(" primer "))
  ln_h(HUB_PRIM)
  ln_s(string(" records "))
  ln_h(HUB_RES)
  ln_s(string("; data end "))
  ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
  ln_s(string("; measuring-cog image "))
  ln_h(@pasm)
  ln_s(string("; last VAR byte array "))
  ln_h(@lineBuf)
  ln_s(string("; cog 0 stack "))
  ln_h(pStack)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("workaround spacing: "))
  ln_waitx()
  ln_s(string(" - the hub instruction after it starts "))
  ln_d(SPACING_CLK)
  ln_s(string(" clocks after the no-wait RDFAST starts (RDFAST "))
  ln_d(RDFAST_CLK)
  ln_s(string(" + WAITX "))
  ln_d(WAITX_BASE)
  ln_c("+")
  ln_d(HUB_SPACING_WAITX)
  say(string(")"))
  say(string("record per trial: v1 = the trial's read (image W: the immediate read-back check; K_CLK: elapsed clocks; PS: the RFLONG), v2 = the long at the address read again after >= 200 clocks, flags = C + 2*Z from the trial's RDLONG ... WCZ (preset C=1 Z=1)"))
  say(string("row codes: image R cell = v1 code + flags code; image W cell = v1 code + v2 code + flags code. O old  N new  P primer  S sentinel  D seed (never written)  F stream long  U unwritten  X other  . right (K_CLK, PS) | flags: digit C+2*Z  - no WCZ  ? other"))
  say(string("agree: . all 16 identical, else hex count identical to rep 0. delta = (a - af) mod 8. Every run: 16 repetitions x 64 cells = 1024 records"))
  ln_s(string("PREDICT controls (MUST, else RIG FAIL): K_CLK elapsed "))
  ln_d(CLK_PRED)
  say(string(" in all 1024 | C1 sentinel C=0 Z=0 in all 1024 | PS the stream's first long $1E1E_0000+af in all 1024 | C3 (new,new) in all 1024"))
  ln_s(string("PREDICT positive controls (else the verdicts they gate are INCONCLUSIVE): P_READ per repetition 43 primer C=1 Z=0 by delta "))
  ln_row8(@predRel)
  ln_s(string(" + 21 sentinel C=0 Z=0 | P_WRITE per repetition 43 (old,old) by delta "))
  ln_row8(@predRel)
  say(string(" + 21 (primer,new)"))
  say(string("PREDICT workarounds (any other record = REFUTED): W_READ sentinel C=0 Z=0 in all 1024 | W_WRITE (new,new) in all 1024 | W_WAIT (new,new) C=1 Z=0 in all 1024 | W_WRBYTE+0..+3, W_WRWORD+0, +2 (merged,merged) in all 1024 each"))
  say(string("rig fails: a record left $EEEE_EEEE in any run; an image R v2 not the sentinel; a control not right in every record; the nowait register echoed back as anything but $8000_0000"))

PRI fill_regions() | idx
' Write every constant data region its pattern.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_STRM][idx] := STRM_V + idx
  longfill(HUB_TBL, SENTV, NSLOT)
  longfill(HUB_WTBL, OLDV, NSLOT)
  long[HUB_PRIM] := PRIMV

PRI region_damage() : damageCnt | idx
' Count read-only data longs that no longer hold their pattern.
'
' @returns damageCnt - changed longs (stream, read table, primer)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  damageCnt := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_STRM][idx] <> STRM_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if long[HUB_TBL][idx] <> SENTV
      damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIM] <> PRIMV
    damageCnt++

PRI reset_tallies()
' Clear every tally.
'

  longfill(@kindCnt, 0, NRUN * NKIND)
  longfill(@rep0Kind, 0, NRUN * NKIND)
  longfill(@runDelta, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDisagree, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runBadCells, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runUnwr, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runTableBad, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runEcho, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runBadRec, -1, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOthRec, -1, NRUN)
  runDamage := 0
  clkMin := POSX
  clkMax := NEGX

PRI send_cmd(runIdx) : status | startCt
' Hand one run to the measuring cog and wait for it to clear MB_CMD.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns status - SUCCESS; E_RIG_FAIL on a 1 s timeout; E_MODE_FAIL (after
'   printing its RIG FAIL line) when the nowait echo is not $8000_0000

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the command was issued

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_COPY] := run_copy(runIdx)
  mbox[MB_OLD] := run_old(runIdx)
  mbox[MB_WVAL] := run_wval(runIdx)
  mbox[MB_OFFS] := run_offs(runIdx)
  mbox[MB_ECHO] := UNWRITTEN
  if run_is_r(runIdx)
    mbox[MB_CMD] := CMD_R
  else
    mbox[MB_CMD] := CMD_W
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_CMD] == 0
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      status := E_RIG_FAIL
      quit
  if status == SUCCESS and mbox[MB_ECHO] <> FIFO_NO_WAIT
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: run "))
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(" ran with the nowait register at "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_ECHO])
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(FIFO_NO_WAIT)
    say(string(" (echo)"))
    status := E_MODE_FAIL

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' run tables
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI run_is_r(runIdx) : bImageR
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bImageR - TRUE for an image R (read) run

  bImageR := runIdx == RUN_KCLK or runIdx == RUN_C1 or runIdx == RUN_PS or runIdx == RUN_PREAD or runIdx == RUN_WREAD

PRI run_copy(runIdx) : copyIdx
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns copyIdx - the measuring cog's trial copy for the run

  copyIdx := lookupz(runIdx: RCOPY_KCLK, RCOPY_C1, RCOPY_PS, WCOPY_C3, RCOPY_PREAD, RCOPY_WREAD, WCOPY_PWRITE, WCOPY_WWRITE, WCOPY_WWAIT, WCOPY_WBYTE, WCOPY_WBYTE, WCOPY_WBYTE, WCOPY_WBYTE, WCOPY_WWORD, WCOPY_WWORD)

PRI run_name(runIdx) : pName
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns pName - printable run name

  pName := lookupz(runIdx: string("K_CLK"), string("C1"), string("PS"), string("C3"), string("P_READ"), string("W_READ"), string("P_WRITE"), string("W_WRITE"), string("W_WAIT"), string("W_WRBYTE+0"), string("W_WRBYTE+1"), string("W_WRBYTE+2"), string("W_WRBYTE+3"), string("W_WRWORD+0"), string("W_WRWORD+2"))

PRI run_size(runIdx) : sizeBytes
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns sizeBytes - bytes the run's write writes (image R: SIZE_LONG, unused)

  if runIdx >= RUN_WB0 and runIdx <= RUN_WB3
    sizeBytes := SIZE_BYTE
  elseif runIdx == RUN_WW0 or runIdx == RUN_WW2
    sizeBytes := SIZE_WORD
  else
    sizeBytes := SIZE_LONG

PRI run_offs(runIdx) : offsBytes
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns offsBytes - byte offset of the write inside the target long

  if runIdx >= RUN_WB0 and runIdx <= RUN_WB3
    offsBytes := runIdx - RUN_WB0
  elseif runIdx == RUN_WW2
    offsBytes := SIZE_WORD
  else
    offsBytes := 0

PRI run_old(runIdx) : oldLong
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns oldLong - the long the target holds before the trial

  if run_size(runIdx) == SIZE_LONG
    oldLong := OLDV
  else
    oldLong := OLDBW

PRI run_wval(runIdx) : dataVal
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns dataVal - the write data register

  if run_size(runIdx) == SIZE_LONG
    dataVal := NEWV
  else
    dataVal := DATABW

PRI run_new(runIdx) : newLong | laneMask, shiftBits
' The long the target holds once the write has landed: the new long, or the
' old long with the written byte / word lanes replaced.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns newLong - the expected long after the write

' Local Variables:
' @local laneMask - $FF or $FFFF
' @local shiftBits - the lane's bit position

  if run_size(runIdx) == SIZE_LONG
    newLong := NEWV
  else
    laneMask := (1 << (run_size(runIdx) * BITS_PER_BYTE)) - 1
    shiftBits := run_offs(runIdx) * BITS_PER_BYTE
    newLong := (OLDBW & !(laneMask << shiftBits)) | ((DATABW & laneMask) << shiftBits)

PRI run_has_flags(runIdx) : bFlags
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bFlags - TRUE when the trial's RDLONG has WCZ (flags preset, then recorded)

  bFlags := runIdx == RUN_C1 or runIdx == RUN_PREAD or runIdx == RUN_WREAD or runIdx == RUN_WWAIT

PRI run_uses_nowait(runIdx) : bNoWait
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bNoWait - TRUE when the trial runs rdfast nowait, hub_stream

  bNoWait := not (runIdx == RUN_KCLK or runIdx == RUN_C1 or runIdx == RUN_C3 or runIdx == RUN_WWAIT)

PRI is_positive(runIdx) : bPositive
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bPositive - TRUE for the positive controls P_READ and P_WRITE

  bPositive := runIdx == RUN_PREAD or runIdx == RUN_PWRITE

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' classification
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI flags_of(datum) : flagsVal
' The flags a RDLONG ... WCZ of this long writes, as recorded.
'
' @param datum - the long
' @returns flagsVal - C (bit 31 of the long) + 2 * Z (the long is zero)

  flagsVal := datum >> LONG_MSB
  if datum == 0
    flagsVal |= 1 << FLAG_Z_BIT

PRI exp_fl(runIdx, datum) : flagsVal
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param datum - the long
' @returns flagsVal - the flags record a trial whose read returned this long leaves

  if run_has_flags(runIdx)
    flagsVal := flags_of(datum)
  else
    flagsVal := FLAGS_NONE

PRI clean_v1(runIdx, afIdx) : cleanVal
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param afIdx - stream slot bits af
' @returns cleanVal - image R: the v1 predicted when nothing completes early

  if runIdx == RUN_KCLK
    cleanVal := CLK_PRED
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS
    cleanVal := STRM_V + afIdx
  else
    cleanVal := SENTV

PRI kind_of(runIdx, afIdx, recV1, recV2, recFl) : kind | newLong, oldLong
' Name one record: clean, completed early (and how), or other.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param afIdx - stream slot bits af
' @param recV1 - the record's first long
' @param recV2 - the record's second long
' @param recFl - the flags long of a record
' @returns kind - KD_*

' Local Variables:
' @local newLong - image W: the long after the write
' @local oldLong - image W: the long before the write

  kind := KD_OTHER
  if run_is_r(runIdx)
    if recV1 == clean_v1(runIdx, afIdx) and recFl == exp_fl(runIdx, recV1)
      kind := KD_CLEAN
    elseif run_has_flags(runIdx) and recV1 == PRIMV and recFl == exp_fl(runIdx, PRIMV)
      kind := KD_REL
  else
    newLong := run_new(runIdx)
    oldLong := run_old(runIdx)
    if recV1 == newLong and recV2 == newLong and recFl == exp_fl(runIdx, newLong)
      kind := KD_CLEAN
    elseif recV1 == oldLong and recV2 == oldLong and recFl == exp_fl(runIdx, oldLong)
      kind := KD_REL
    elseif recV1 == PRIMV and recV2 == newLong and recFl == exp_fl(runIdx, PRIMV)
      kind := KD_RDREL

PRI class_v(runIdx, afIdx, datum) : cls
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param afIdx - stream slot bits af
' @param datum - the long
' @returns cls - the value class (VC_*) of the long

  if runIdx == RUN_KCLK
    if datum == CLK_PRED
      cls := VC_RIGHT
    elseif datum == UNWRITTEN
      cls := VC_UNWR
    else
      cls := VC_OTHER
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS and datum == STRM_V + afIdx
    cls := VC_RIGHT
  elseif not run_is_r(runIdx) and datum == run_old(runIdx)
    cls := VC_OLD
  elseif not run_is_r(runIdx) and datum == run_new(runIdx)
    cls := VC_NEW
  elseif datum == PRIMV
    cls := VC_PRIM
  elseif datum == SENTV
    cls := VC_SENT
  elseif datum == SEEDV
    cls := VC_SEED
  elseif datum == UNWRITTEN
    cls := VC_UNWR
  elseif (datum - STRM_V) +< STRM_LONGS
    cls := VC_STRM
  else
    cls := VC_OTHER

PRI vcchar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - the value class (VC_*)
' @returns codeChar - O N P D S F U X .

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: "O", "N", "P", "D", "S", "F", "U", "X", ".")

PRI flchar(recFl) : codeChar
' @param recFl - the flags long of a record
' @returns codeChar - digit C+2*Z, "-" no WCZ, "U" never written, "?" other

  if recFl == FLAGS_NONE
    codeChar := "-"
  elseif recFl +< FLAG_CODES
    codeChar := "0" + recFl
  elseif recFl == UNWRITTEN
    codeChar := "U"
  else
    codeChar := "?"

PRI agreechar(agreeCnt) : codeChar
' @param agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (1..16)
' @returns codeChar - "." for all 16, else the hex digit

  if agreeCnt == REPS
    codeChar := "."
  elseif agreeCnt < 10
    codeChar := "0" + agreeCnt
  else
    codeChar := "A" + agreeCnt - 10

PRI cell_delta(cellIdx) : deltaIdx
' @param cellIdx - af * 8 + a
' @returns deltaIdx - (a - af) mod 8

  deltaIdx := ((cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1)) - (cellIdx / NSLOT)) & (NSLOT - 1)

PRI rec_addr(recIdx) : pRec
' @param recIdx - record index: rep * 64 + af * 8 + a
' @returns pRec - hub address of the record

  pRec := HUB_RES + recIdx * RECW * 4

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' one run: classify and print
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI process_run(runIdx) | cellIdx, afIdx, repIdx, recIdx, pRec, firstV1, firstV2, firstFl, recV1, recV2, recFl, kind, agreeCnt, notCleanCnt
' Classify a run: repetition-0 codes and kinds, agreement, totals, delta split,
' the first record not clean and the first of a kind not named.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + a
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits af
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local recIdx - record index
' @local pRec - hub address of the record
' @local firstV1 - repetition 0's v1
' @local firstV2 - repetition 0's v2
' @local firstFl - repetition 0's flags
' @local recV1 - the record's first long
' @local recV2 - the record's second long
' @local recFl - the flags long of a record
' @local kind - the record's kind (KD_*)
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local notCleanCnt - repetitions not clean

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    afIdx := cellIdx / NSLOT
    pRec := rec_addr(cellIdx)
    firstV1 := long[pRec][REC_V1]
    firstV2 := long[pRec][REC_V2]
    firstFl := long[pRec][REC_FL]
    cellV1[cellIdx] := class_v(runIdx, afIdx, firstV1)
    cellV2[cellIdx] := class_v(runIdx, afIdx, firstV2)
    cellFl[cellIdx] := flchar(firstFl)
    kind := kind_of(runIdx, afIdx, firstV1, firstV2, firstFl)
    rep0Kind[runIdx * NKIND + kind]++
    if kind == KD_REL
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    notCleanCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      recIdx := repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx
      pRec := rec_addr(recIdx)
      recV1 := long[pRec][REC_V1]
      recV2 := long[pRec][REC_V2]
      recFl := long[pRec][REC_FL]
      kind := kind_of(runIdx, afIdx, recV1, recV2, recFl)
      kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + kind]++
      if kind <> KD_CLEAN
        notCleanCnt++
        if runBadRec[runIdx] == -1 or recIdx < runBadRec[runIdx]
          runBadRec[runIdx] := recIdx
          runBadV1[runIdx] := recV1
          runBadV2[runIdx] := recV2
          runBadFl[runIdx] := recFl
      if kind == KD_OTHER and (runOthRec[runIdx] == -1 or recIdx < runOthRec[runIdx])
        runOthRec[runIdx] := recIdx
        runOthV1[runIdx] := recV1
        runOthV2[runIdx] := recV2
        runOthFl[runIdx] := recFl
      if recV1 == UNWRITTEN or recV2 == UNWRITTEN or recFl == UNWRITTEN
        runUnwr[runIdx]++
      if run_is_r(runIdx) and recV2 <> SENTV
        runTableBad[runIdx]++
      if runIdx == RUN_KCLK
        clkMin <#= recV1
        clkMax #>= recV1
      if recV1 == firstV1 and recV2 == firstV2 and recFl == firstFl
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    cellNotClean[cellIdx] := notCleanCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++
    if notCleanCnt > 0
      runBadCells[runIdx]++

PRI print_run_header(runIdx)
' Print the run's instructions and its prediction before its rows.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

  if runIdx == RUN_KCLK
    ln_s(string("RUN K_CLK (CONTROL): getct / "))
    ln_waitx()
    ln_s(string(" / getct. MUST: elapsed "))
    ln_d(CLK_PRED)
    say(string(" (GETCT 2 + WAITX 2+D) in all 1024 trials, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_C1
    say(string("RUN C1 (CONTROL, image R): modcz C=1 Z=1 / rdlong primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST / rdlong value,hub_addr WCZ. MUST: the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS
    ln_s(string("RUN PS (CONTROL, image R): rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / waitx #200 / rflong value. MUST: the stream's first long $1E1E_0000+af in all 1024 records, "))
    say(string("else RIG FAIL (the RDFAST under test would not be starting a stream)"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_C3
    say(string("RUN C3 (CONTROL, image W): rdlong primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST / wrlong value,hub_addr / rdlong check,hub_addr ... later read. MUST: (new,new) in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PREAD
    ln_s(string("RUN P_READ (POSITIVE CONTROL, image R): modcz C=1 Z=1 / rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / rdlong value,hub_addr WCZ. PREDICT per repetition: 43 primer C=1 Z=0 by delta "))
    ln_row8(@predRel)
    say(string(" + 21 sentinel C=0 Z=0"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_WREAD
    ln_s(string("RUN W_READ (WORKAROUND, the printed read block, image R): modcz C=1 Z=1 / rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / "))
    ln_waitx()
    say(string(" / rdlong value,hub_addr WCZ. PREDICT: the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1024 records; any other = REFUTED"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PWRITE
    ln_s(string("RUN P_WRITE (POSITIVE CONTROL, image W): rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / wrlong value,hub_addr / rdlong check,hub_addr ... later read. PREDICT per repetition: 43 (old,old) by delta "))
    ln_row8(@predRel)
    say(string(" + 21 (primer,new)"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_WWRITE
    ln_s(string("RUN W_WRITE (WORKAROUND, the printed write block, image W): rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / "))
    ln_waitx()
    say(string(" / wrlong value,hub_addr / rdlong check,hub_addr ... later read. PREDICT: (new,new) in all 1024 records; any other = REFUTED"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_WWAIT
    ln_s(string("RUN W_WAIT (WORKAROUND, the printed waiting-form block, image W): modcz C=1 Z=1 / rdlong primer / rdfast #0,hub_stream / wrlong value,hub_addr / rdlong check,hub_addr WCZ ... later read. "))
    say(string("PREDICT: (new,new) with C=1 Z=0 in all 1024 records; any other = REFUTED"))
  else
    ln_s(string("RUN "))
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(" (image W): rdlong primer / rdfast nowait,hub_stream / "))
    ln_waitx()
    if run_size(runIdx) == SIZE_BYTE
      ln_s(string(" / wrbyte"))
    else
      ln_s(string(" / wrword"))
    ln_s(string(" value,hub_addr (hub_long+"))
    ln_d(run_offs(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(") / rdlong check,hub_long ... later read. PREDICT: (new,new), the merged long "))
    ln_h(run_new(runIdx))
    say(string(", in all 1024 records; any other = REFUTED"))

PRI print_run(runIdx) | afIdx, arIdx, cellIdx, cellW, base, bImageR
' Print a run's raw rows (repetition 0 per af, agreement) and its totals.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits af
' @local arIdx - address slot bits a
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + a
' @local cellW - row chars per cell
' @local base - index of the run's first count, or of the cell's first row char
' @local bImageR - the run is an image R run

  bImageR := run_is_r(runIdx)
  if bImageR
    cellW := R_CELL_W
  else
    cellW := W_CELL_W
  repeat afIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    repeat arIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      cellIdx := afIdx * NSLOT + arIdx
      agreeStr[arIdx] := agreechar(cellAgree[cellIdx])
      base := arIdx * cellW
      rowStr[base] := vcchar(cellV1[cellIdx])
      if bImageR
        rowStr[base + 1] := cellFl[cellIdx]
      else
        rowStr[base + 1] := vcchar(cellV2[cellIdx])
        rowStr[base + 2] := cellFl[cellIdx]
      rowStr[base + cellW - 1] := " "
    agreeStr[NSLOT] := 0
    rowStr[NSLOT * cellW - 1] := 0
    ln_run(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" af"))
    ln_d(afIdx)
    ln_s(string(" rep0 a0-7: "))
    ln_s(@rowStr)
    ln_s(string("  agree "))
    say(@agreeStr)

  base := runIdx * NKIND
  ln_run(runIdx)
  ln_s(string(" all reps: clean "))
  ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_CLEAN])
  if bImageR
    ln_s(string(" | early (primer) "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_REL])
  else
    ln_s(string(" | (old,old) write lost "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_REL])
    ln_s(string(" | (primer,new) read-back early "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_RDREL])
  ln_s(string(" | other "))
  ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_OTHER])
  ln_s(string(" | of "))
  ln_d(NREC)
  ln_s(string(" | rep0 early cells by delta "))
  ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
  ln_s(string(" = "))
  ln_d(rep0Kind[base + KD_REL])
  if not bImageR
    ln_s(string(", rep0 (primer,new) "))
    ln_d(rep0Kind[base + KD_RDREL])
  ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
  ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
  if run_uses_nowait(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" | nowait (RDFAST D) run "))
    ln_h(runEcho[runIdx])
  if runIdx == RUN_KCLK
    ln_s(string(" | elapsed "))
    ln_d(clkMin)
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(clkMax)
    ln_s(string(" clk (predicted "))
    ln_d(CLK_PRED)
    ln_c(")")
  ln_out()

  if is_positive(runIdx)
    if runOthRec[runIdx] <> -1
      ln_run(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" first record of a kind the prediction does not name: "))
      ln_rec(runOthRec[runIdx], runOthV1[runIdx], runOthV2[runIdx], runOthFl[runIdx])
      ln_out()
  elseif runBadCells[runIdx] > 0
    ln_run(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" cells not clean (af a:reps):"))
    repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
      if cellNotClean[cellIdx] > 0
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_d(cellIdx / NSLOT)
        ln_d(cellIdx // NSLOT)
        ln_c(":")
        ln_d(cellNotClean[cellIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_run(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" first record not clean: "))
    ln_rec(runBadRec[runIdx], runBadV1[runIdx], runBadV2[runIdx], runBadFl[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  if runUnwr[runIdx] > 0
    ln_run(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" records with a long never written (U, $EEEE_EEEE): "))
    ln_d(runUnwr[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  if runTableBad[runIdx] > 0
    ln_run(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" records whose v2 (the read table long after settling) is not the sentinel: "))
    ln_d(runTableBad[runIdx])
    ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' gates and positive controls
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI rig_gate() : bPass | runIdx, ctrlIdx, unwrCnt, tableCnt
' Check every gate after the runs; print a RIG FAIL line for each that fails.
'
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @local ctrlIdx - control index 0..NCTRL-1
' @local unwrCnt - records with a long never written, over every run
' @local tableCnt - image R records whose later read is not the sentinel

  unwrCnt := 0
  tableCnt := 0
  repeat runIdx from 0 to NRUN - 1
    unwrCnt += runUnwr[runIdx]
    tableCnt += runTableBad[runIdx]
  bPass := TRUE
  if unwrCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(unwrCnt)
    say(string(" records hold a long still $EEEE_EEEE: the measuring cog never wrote them"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if tableCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(tableCnt)
    say(string(" image R records read the table long after settling as something other than the sentinel: the read table or the read path is wrong"))
    bPass := FALSE
  repeat ctrlIdx from 0 to NCTRL - 1
    runIdx := lookupz(ctrlIdx: RUN_KCLK, RUN_C1, RUN_PS, RUN_C3)
    if kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_CLEAN] <> NREC
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: control "))
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      ln_s(string(" right in "))
      ln_d(kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_CLEAN])
      ln_s(string(" of "))
      ln_d(NREC)
      ln_s(string(" records (its MUST is on its RUN line); first wrong: "))
      ln_rec(runBadRec[runIdx], runBadV1[runIdx], runBadV2[runIdx], runBadFl[runIdx])
      ln_out()
      bPass := FALSE
  if runDamage > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE: "))
    ln_d(runDamage)
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the runs (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))
  if bPass
    ln_s(string("RIG OK: K_CLK "))
    ln_d(CLK_PRED)
    say(string(" clocks, C1 the sentinel with C=0 Z=0, PS the stream's first long and C3 (new,new) in every record; no record left unwritten; every image R table long intact; nowait echoed $8000_0000 after every run"))

PRI delta_match(runIdx) : bMatch | deltaIdx
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bMatch - TRUE when the run's repetition-0 early cells by delta equal predRel

' Local Variables:
' @local deltaIdx - delta 0..7

  bMatch := TRUE
  repeat deltaIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + deltaIdx] <> predRel[deltaIdx]
      bMatch := FALSE

PRI pos_read() : bRepro | base
' Decide whether P_READ reproduced the erratum; print the evidence.
'
' @returns bRepro - TRUE when P_READ matched its prediction in every record

' Local Variables:
' @local base - index of P_READ's first count

  base := RUN_PREAD * NKIND
  bRepro := kindCnt[base + KD_OTHER] == 0 and runDisagree[RUN_PREAD] == 0 and rep0Kind[base + KD_REL] == PRED_REL and delta_match(RUN_PREAD)
  if bRepro
    ln_s(string("POSITIVE CONTROL P_READ: REPRODUCED - with no spacing, the RDLONG completed early in 43 of 64 cells in every repetition, each returning the primer $A5A5_0001 with C=1 Z=0, by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_PREAD * NSLOT])
    say(string("; the other 21 read the sentinel with C=0 Z=0"))
  else
    ln_s(string("POSITIVE CONTROL P_READ: NOT REPRODUCED - rep0 primer cells "))
    ln_d(rep0Kind[base + KD_REL])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_PREAD * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" (predicted 43 by "))
    ln_row8(@predRel)
    ln_s(string("); records the prediction does not name "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_OTHER])
    ln_s(string("; cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[RUN_PREAD])
    ln_out()

PRI pos_write() : bRepro | base
' Decide whether P_WRITE reproduced the erratum; print the evidence.
'
' @returns bRepro - TRUE when P_WRITE matched its prediction in every record

' Local Variables:
' @local base - index of P_WRITE's first count

  base := RUN_PWRITE * NKIND
  bRepro := kindCnt[base + KD_OTHER] == 0 and runDisagree[RUN_PWRITE] == 0 and rep0Kind[base + KD_REL] == PRED_REL and rep0Kind[base + KD_RDREL] == PRED_RDREL and delta_match(RUN_PWRITE)
  if bRepro
    ln_s(string("POSITIVE CONTROL P_WRITE: REPRODUCED - with no spacing, the write was lost, (old,old), in 43 of 64 cells in every repetition, by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_PWRITE * NSLOT])
    say(string("; in the other 21 the write landed and the read-back returned the primer, (primer,new)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("POSITIVE CONTROL P_WRITE: NOT REPRODUCED - rep0 (old,old) cells "))
    ln_d(rep0Kind[base + KD_REL])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_PWRITE * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(", (primer,new) cells "))
    ln_d(rep0Kind[base + KD_RDREL])
    ln_s(string(" (predicted 43 by "))
    ln_row8(@predRel)
    ln_s(string(" and 21); records the prediction does not name "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[base + KD_OTHER])
    ln_s(string("; cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[RUN_PWRITE])
    ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' verdicts
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_refuted(runIdx)
' Append the evidence of a refuted workaround run: its counts, its cells and
' its first record not clean.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

  ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
  ln_s(string(" clean in "))
  ln_d(kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_CLEAN])
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(NREC)
  ln_s(string(" records (completed early: "))
  ln_d(kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_REL])
  if not run_is_r(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" (old,old), "))
    ln_d(kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_RDREL])
    ln_s(string(" (primer,new)"))
  ln_s(string("; other: "))
  ln_d(kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_OTHER])
  ln_s(string(") in "))
  ln_d(runBadCells[runIdx])
  ln_s(string(" cells (listed under RUN "))
  ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
  ln_s(string("); first: "))
  ln_rec(runBadRec[runIdx], runBadV1[runIdx], runBadV2[runIdx], runBadFl[runIdx])

PRI verdict_read(bRigOk, bRepro)
' VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRigOk - every gate passed
' @param bRepro - the positive control reproduced the erratum

  if not bRigOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ: NO VERDICT - a gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
  elseif kindCnt[RUN_WREAD * NKIND + KD_CLEAN] <> NREC
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ: REFUTED - "))
    ln_refuted(RUN_WREAD)
    ln_out()
  elseif not bRepro
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ: INCONCLUSIVE - W_READ read the sentinel with C=0 Z=0 in all 1024 records, but P_READ did not reproduce the erratum in this run (see POSITIVE CONTROL P_READ), so the clean result is not shown beating it"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND READ: CONFIRMED - with "))
    ln_waitx()
    ln_s(string(" the RDLONG started "))
    ln_d(SPACING_CLK)
    ln_s(string(" clocks after the no-wait RDFAST and read the sentinel $5A5A_0002 with C=0 Z=0 in all "))
    ln_d(NREC)
    say(string(" records (64 alignments x 16); P_READ in the same run, with no spacing, completed early in 43 of 64 cells per repetition"))

PRI verdict_write(bRigOk, bRepro)
' VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRigOk - every gate passed
' @param bRepro - the positive control reproduced the erratum

  if not bRigOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: NO VERDICT - a gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
  elseif kindCnt[RUN_WWRITE * NKIND + KD_CLEAN] <> NREC
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: REFUTED - "))
    ln_refuted(RUN_WWRITE)
    ln_out()
  elseif not bRepro
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: INCONCLUSIVE - W_WRITE gave (new,new) in all 1024 records, but P_WRITE did not reproduce the erratum in this run (see POSITIVE CONTROL P_WRITE), so the clean result is not shown beating it"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: CONFIRMED - with "))
    ln_waitx()
    ln_s(string(" the WRLONG started "))
    ln_d(SPACING_CLK)
    ln_s(string(" clocks after the no-wait RDFAST; its write landed and the RDLONG after it read it back: (new,new) $F0F0_0005 in all "))
    ln_d(NREC)
    say(string(" records (64 alignments x 16); P_WRITE in the same run, with no spacing, lost the write in 43 of 64 cells per repetition"))

PRI verdict_waiting(bRigOk, bRepro)
' VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRigOk - every gate passed
' @param bRepro - the positive control reproduced the erratum

  if not bRigOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING: NO VERDICT - a gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
  elseif kindCnt[RUN_WWAIT * NKIND + KD_CLEAN] <> NREC
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING: REFUTED - "))
    ln_refuted(RUN_WWAIT)
    ln_out()
  elseif not bRepro
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING: INCONCLUSIVE - W_WAIT gave (new,new) with C=1 Z=0 in all 1024 records, but P_WRITE did not reproduce the erratum in this run (see POSITIVE CONTROL P_WRITE), so the clean result is not shown beating it"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND WAITING: CONFIRMED - with the waiting RDFAST (D = 0) and no spacing, the WRLONG's write landed and the RDLONG after it read it back with its flags: (new,new) $F0F0_0005 with C=1 Z=0 in all "))
    ln_d(NREC)
    say(string(" records (64 alignments x 16); P_WRITE in the same run, with the no-wait form, lost the write in 43 of 64 cells per repetition"))

PRI verdict_bytes(bRigOk, bRepro) | runIdx, badCnt
' VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRigOk - every gate passed
' @param bRepro - the positive control reproduced the erratum

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @local badCnt - records not clean over the six byte / word runs

  badCnt := 0
  repeat runIdx from RUN_WB0 to RUN_WW2
    badCnt += NREC - kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_CLEAN]
  if not bRigOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES: NO VERDICT - a gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
  elseif badCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES: REFUTED - records not the merged long (read back at once and read later), of 1024 per run:"))
    repeat runIdx from RUN_WB0 to RUN_WW2
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_d(NREC - kindCnt[runIdx * NKIND + KD_CLEAN])
    say(string(" (cells and first record under each run)"))
  elseif not bRepro
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES: INCONCLUSIVE - every byte and word run left the merged long in all 1024 records, but P_WRITE did not reproduce the erratum in this run (see POSITIVE CONTROL P_WRITE), so the clean result is not shown beating it"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WORKAROUND BYTE/WORD WRITES: CONFIRMED - with "))
    ln_waitx()
    ln_s(string(", WRBYTE at offsets 0..3 and WRWORD at offsets 0 and 2, each started "))
    ln_d(SPACING_CLK)
    ln_s(string(" clocks after the no-wait RDFAST, left the merged long, read back at once and read later, in all "))
    ln_d(NREC)
    say(string(" records of each of the six runs; P_WRITE in the same run, with no spacing, lost the write in 43 of 64 cells per repetition"))

DAT ' ---- Predictions (printed in the header before the run) ----
' Positive controls: early cells per repetition by delta 0..7 (43 in all)
predRel         long    8, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug(), no BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it).
' From each primer RDLONG to the last instruction under test there is
' nothing but the run's instructions; no ## operand.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            mov     c_tmp, ##STAT_READY
                wrlong  c_tmp, ptra[MB_ALIVE]

wait_cmd        rdlong  c_cmd, ptra                     wz      ' MB_CMD: 0 = idle
        if_z    jmp     #wait_cmd
                rdlong  c_copy, ptra[MB_COPY]
                rdlong  c_oldv, ptra[MB_OLD]
                rdlong  c_wval, ptra[MB_WVAL]
                rdlong  c_offs, ptra[MB_OFFS]
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_R                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #run_r
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_W                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #run_w
cmd_done        wrlong  nowait, ptra[MB_ECHO]                   ' epilogue, after every record: echo nowait
                wrlong  #0, ptra                                ' MB_CMD := 0 -> done
                jmp     #wait_cmd

'--- image R: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 a; record (rep*8 + af)*8 + a
run_r           alts    c_copy, #rvec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
r_rep           mov     c_af, #0
r_af            mov     c_ar, #0
r_ar            mov     hub_stream, c_af
                shl     hub_stream, #2
                add     hub_stream, c_strm                      ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     hub_addr, c_ar
                shl     hub_addr, #2
                add     hub_addr, c_tbl                         ' read address: slot bits = a
                mov     value, c_seedv                          ' "never written" stays visible
                mov     c_flags, #FLAGS_NONE                    ' no WCZ: stays $FF
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
r_settle        mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
r_dly           djnz    c_t, #r_dly                             ' >= 200 clocks: everything settles
                rdlong  c_later, hub_addr                       ' the table long, read again
                wrlong  value, c_rp                             ' record: v1, v2, flags
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_later, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_flags, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_af
                djnz    c_reps, #r_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image R trial copies
t_kclk          getct   c_t0                                    ' K_CLK: the spacing WAITX alone
                waitx   #HUB_SPACING_WAITX                      ' K_CLK: the printed blocks' WAITX
                getct   c_t1
                mov     value, c_t1
                sub     value, c_t0                             ' K_CLK: elapsed = GETCT 2 + WAITX 2+D
                jmp     #r_settle

t_c1            modcz   _set, _set                      wcz     ' C1: flags preset C=1 Z=1
                rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' C1: primer
                nop                                             ' C1: NOP in place of the RDFAST
                rdlong  value, hub_addr                 wcz     ' C1: the RDLONG, nothing before it
                wrc     c_flags                                 ' C1: C into flags bit 0
                bitz    c_flags, #FLAG_Z_BIT                    ' C1: Z into flags bit 1
                jmp     #r_settle

t_ps            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' PS: primer
                rdfast  nowait, hub_stream                      ' PS: the RDFAST under test
                waitx   #STREAM_WAIT                            ' PS: long past any start-up
                rflong  value                                   ' PS: the stream's first long
                jmp     #r_settle

t_pread         modcz   _set, _set                      wcz     ' P_READ: flags preset C=1 Z=1
                rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' P_READ: primer
                rdfast  nowait, hub_stream                      ' P_READ: no-wait RDFAST
                rdlong  value, hub_addr                 wcz     ' P_READ: the RDLONG at once
                wrc     c_flags
                bitz    c_flags, #FLAG_Z_BIT
                jmp     #r_settle

t_wread         modcz   _set, _set                      wcz     ' W_READ: flags preset C=1 Z=1
                rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' W_READ: primer
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND READ: begin (Erratum E7 prints these) ----
        rdfast  nowait, hub_stream      ' no-wait RDFAST (D[31] = 1)
        waitx   #HUB_SPACING_WAITX      ' E7: >= 16 clocks to next hub op
        rdlong  value, hub_addr  wcz    ' hub_addr's long, and its flags
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND READ: end ----
                wrc     c_flags                                 ' W_READ: C into flags bit 0
                bitz    c_flags, #FLAG_Z_BIT                    ' W_READ: Z into flags bit 1
                jmp     #r_settle

'--- image W: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 a; records check, later, flags per trial
run_w           alts    c_copy, #wvec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
w_rep           mov     c_af, #0
w_af            mov     c_ar, #0
w_ar            mov     hub_stream, c_af
                shl     hub_stream, #2
                add     hub_stream, c_strm                      ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     hub_long, c_ar
                shl     hub_long, #2
                add     hub_long, c_wtbl                        ' target long: slot bits = a
                mov     hub_addr, hub_long
                add     hub_addr, c_offs                        ' the write's byte address
                wrlong  c_oldv, hub_long                        ' the target holds the old long
                mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
w_d1            djnz    c_t, #w_d1
                mov     check, c_seedv
                mov     c_later, c_seedv
                mov     value, c_wval                           ' the write data
                mov     c_flags, #FLAGS_NONE                    ' no WCZ: stays $FF
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
w_settle        mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
w_d2            djnz    c_t, #w_d2
                rdlong  c_later, hub_long                       ' read-back after everything settled
                wrlong  check, c_rp                             ' record: v1, v2, flags
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_later, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_flags, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_af
                djnz    c_reps, #w_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image W trial copies
t_c3            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' C3: primer
                nop                                             ' C3: NOP in place of the RDFAST
                wrlong  value, hub_addr                         ' C3: the WRLONG
                rdlong  check, hub_addr                         ' C3: immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle

t_pwrite        rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' P_WRITE: primer
                rdfast  nowait, hub_stream                      ' P_WRITE: no-wait RDFAST
                wrlong  value, hub_addr                         ' P_WRITE: the WRLONG at once
                rdlong  check, hub_addr                         ' P_WRITE: immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle

t_wwrite        rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' W_WRITE: primer
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: begin (Erratum E7 prints these) ----
        rdfast  nowait, hub_stream      ' no-wait RDFAST (D[31] = 1)
        waitx   #HUB_SPACING_WAITX      ' E7: >= 16 clocks to next hub op
        wrlong  value, hub_addr         ' lands at hub_addr
        rdlong  check, hub_addr         ' the next hub instruction
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND WRITE: end ----
                jmp     #w_settle

t_wwait         modcz   _set, _set                      wcz     ' W_WAIT: flags preset C=1 Z=1
                rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' W_WAIT: primer
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND WAITING FORM: begin (Erratum E7 prints these) ----
        rdfast  #0, hub_stream          ' waiting RDFAST (D[31] = 0)
        wrlong  value, hub_addr         ' lands at hub_addr
        rdlong  check, hub_addr  wcz    ' reads value back, and its flags
' ---- E7 WORKAROUND WAITING FORM: end ----
                wrc     c_flags                                 ' W_WAIT: C into flags bit 0
                bitz    c_flags, #FLAG_Z_BIT                    ' W_WAIT: Z into flags bit 1
                jmp     #w_settle

t_wbyte         rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' W_WRBYTE: primer
                rdfast  nowait, hub_stream                      ' W_WRBYTE: no-wait RDFAST
                waitx   #HUB_SPACING_WAITX                      ' W_WRBYTE: the workaround spacing
                wrbyte  value, hub_addr                         ' W_WRBYTE: byte $FB at the offset
                rdlong  check, hub_long                         ' W_WRBYTE: the whole long, at once
                jmp     #w_settle

t_wword         rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' W_WRWORD: primer
                rdfast  nowait, hub_stream                      ' W_WRWORD: no-wait RDFAST
                waitx   #HUB_SPACING_WAITX                      ' W_WRWORD: the workaround spacing
                wrword  value, hub_addr                         ' W_WRWORD: word $EAFB at the offset
                rdlong  check, hub_long                         ' W_WRWORD: the whole long, at once
                jmp     #w_settle

'--- trial-copy vectors
rvec_tab        long    t_kclk, t_c1, t_ps, t_pread, t_wread            ' RCOPY_* order
wvec_tab        long    t_c3, t_pwrite, t_wwrite, t_wwait, t_wbyte, t_wword ' WCOPY_* order

'--- cog data.  nowait, hub_stream, hub_addr, value and check are named in the printed blocks.
nowait          long    FIFO_NO_WAIT                            ' RDFAST D: D[31]=1 no-wait, block count 0 (no wrap)
hub_stream      long    0                                       ' the RDFAST's address: stream slot bits af
hub_addr        long    0                                       ' the read / write address under test
hub_long        long    0                                       ' image W: the target long (read-back address)
value           long    0                                       ' image R: the read; image W: the write data
check           long    0                                       ' image W: the immediate read-back
c_strm          long    HUB_STRM
c_tbl           long    HUB_TBL
c_wtbl          long    HUB_WTBL
c_prim          long    HUB_PRIM
c_res           long    HUB_RES
c_seedv         long    SEEDV
c_oldv          long    0                                       ' image W: the old long (MB_OLD)
c_wval          long    0                                       ' image W: the write data (MB_WVAL)
c_offs          long    0                                       ' image W: byte offset of the write (MB_OFFS)
c_later         long    0                                       ' the address read again after settling
c_flags         long    0                                       ' recorded flags: C bit 0, Z bit 1, $FF none
c_cmd           long    0
c_copy          long    0
c_vec           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_reps          long    0
c_af            long    0
c_ar            long    0
c_t             long    0
c_t0            long    0
c_t1            long    0
c_tmp           long    0
pasm_end

